    "body": "The last unresolved #393 program row, confirmed unstarted (the 'private track' never ran — Casey, 2026-08-05). **Claim to test:** building the store/cover in structural strata (partitioned construction) beats one flat construction on held-out, graded against #391 null discipline. **Why it matters more now:** the #399 falsifier-2 record shows the substrate scores 36.5% when construction is effectively stratified (few deeply-observed topics) and ~26% when one flat construction spans 10,000 topics at ANY measured capacity — the corpus-composition finding is plausibly a stratification effect. If per-stratum construction + stratum routing recovers the redundancy-regime numbers on the broad corpus, this is THE mechanism for #433's ceiling. First measurement: partition wiki10k construction by story/topic clusters (e.g., per-story or k-cluster strata), build per-stratum stores, route held-out queries to strata (oracle-stratum arm = ceiling; routed-stratum arm = the claim; flat arm = the measured 26% baseline), grade with pre-declared exit rule. The #432 env knobs and existing harnesses make this cheap to stand up.",
