      "created_at": "2026-08-06T01:26:29Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-06T01:26:29Z",
      "body": "Growth law + criterion sweep (PR #445, harness in #444). The class count does NOT saturate: distinct left keys ~n^0.44, distribution-signature classes ~n^0.46 (left) / ~n^0.80 (two-sided) across a 17× data range, with mean support per class rising 7.3→35.6 (genuine structure, not noise-splitting). Criterion sweep at 2.11M records: fixed-θ relative FAILS (H(parent) grows 6.52→9.65 bits so θ·H becomes a stricter bar, cover collapses to 8 regions), MDL FAILS, and only the capacity law k0_eff = k0·(n/n_ref)^0.45 is monotone (14→23→25 regions) while beating baseline held-out top-1 (0.0470 vs 0.0438). Conclusion: scale capacity, don't tune thresholds.",
